{
  "_notes": [
    "Derived from native NVRAM offsets.",
    "This map focuses on current/last game score extraction.",
    "Verify score encoding/scale with real NVRAM before production use.",
    "Player score fields currently mirror top saved score slots until per-player RAM offsets are mapped."
  ],
  "_fileformat": 0.7,
  "_metadata": {
    "version": 4,
    "platform": "capcom",
    "roms": [
      "pmv112",
      "pmv112r"
    ]
  },
  "game_state": {
    "final_scores_order": "most_recent_first",
    "final_scores": [
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 1 (newest)",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001EF6",
          "0x30001EF8",
          "0x30001EFA",
          "0x30001EFC"
        ],
        "_notes": [
          "Recent-games buffer in battery DRAM (.nv file offset 0x1EF6), newest completed entry first; one push per player at game over, last player first. Verified with a real 4-player game (P1 62,576,260 / P2 18,396,190 / P3 15,376,900 / P4 17,265,150 read back as entries 4..1 exactly). Title-specific base (bbb109 0x205E, bsv103 0x1EEA). No usable player_count byte is known; the plugin infers the player count from entries pushed on top of the session-start baseline."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 2",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001EFE",
          "0x30001F00",
          "0x30001F02",
          "0x30001F04"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 3",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001F06",
          "0x30001F08",
          "0x30001F0A",
          "0x30001F0C"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Recent Game 4 (oldest)",
        "encoding": "int",
        "endian": "big",
        "scale": 10,
        "offsets": [
          "0x30001F0E",
          "0x30001F10",
          "0x30001F12",
          "0x30001F14"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "credits": {
      "label": "Credits",
      "start": "0x30000010",
      "encoding": "int",
      "length": 1,
      "_notes": [
        "Battery DRAM, platform-wide: verified against user-reported credit counts on bbb109 (7), bsv103 (5) and pmv112 (4), and observed incrementing on coin insertion in a headless probe. (0x3000139C, previously mapped, is a different counter that only coincidentally matched on bbb/bsv.)"
      ]
    },
    "game_over": {
      "_notes": [
        "Game-in-progress flag in DRAM (volatile RAM, not in the .nv). Found via libpinmame, verified across Breakshot/Big Bang Bar/Pinball Magic: 0x000012F2 bit 0x40 is SET during a game, CLEAR in attract and at game over. invert=true so the field reads true when the game is over."
      ],
      "label": "Game Over",
      "start": "0x000012F2",
      "encoding": "bool",
      "mask": "0x40",
      "invert": true
    },
    "_notes": [
      "scores was removed: all four player entries aliased the NVRAM high-score mirror at 0x300000F0, so they reported leaderboard values instead of the game being played. Capcom keeps live scores in volatile DRAM (verified for bbb109 Player 1 at 0x00061F32); each game needs its own verified address before scores can be reinstated."
    ]
  },
